WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.080
The MCU is more than a decade into its run,
but there are countless Marvel characters

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:07.500
whose origins still haven't been told on the
big screen.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:10.260
So which characters actually deserve to make
the leap?

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:14.900
From Britain’s guardian to a worthy space
horse, here are the Marvel origin stories

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:16.820
we'd love to see on film.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:19.440
Most of the X-Men's origin stories are simple.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.980
They were born with the X-gene, developed
their uncanny mutant abilities in their teens

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:26.740
and then Professor X found them, or some version
of that.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:31.259
Then there are the mutants who led rich, exciting
lives well before joining the X-Men, like

00:00:31.259 --> 00:00:33.140
Wolverine, or Deadpool, or Gambit.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:37.980
Two of those three have gotten their own films,
and a Gambit movie was in the works for years.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:42.290
Then, Disney's purchase of Fox seemed to kill
it, and that's a shame, because his incredible

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:44.980
origin story definitely deserves some screen
time.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:47.660
"Are you Remy Lebeau?"

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:51.300
"Do I owe you money?"

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:56.140
Remy LeBeau was abandoned as a baby because
part of his mutation, his glowing red eyes,

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:57.600
was already visible at birth.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:02.760
He was then adopted as a kind of prophesied
savior by the New Orleans Thieves Guild and

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.430
was raised to be a master thief.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:08.479
Then, an arranged marriage within the guilds
led to a duel, the murder of a member of the

00:01:08.479 --> 00:01:12.890
Assassins Guild, and an excommunication from
the Thieves Guild, which ultimately brought

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:13.980
Remy to the X-Men.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:18.119
It's complex, it's dramatic, and it's got
lots of opportunities for John Wick-style

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:20.240
action set in the heart of New Orleans.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:24.200
Even if you're sick of origin story movies,
this one might win you over.

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:29.499
Sometimes the best way to lay out a superhero
origin story is to keep things as vague as

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:30.000
possible.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:34.259
That's always been the case with the unbeatable
Squirrel Girl, a beloved heroine whose name

00:01:34.259 --> 00:01:38.539
gives you a very good idea of her power set,
but doesn't really explain why she can take

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:41.160
down literally any bad guy in the Marvel Universe.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:45.219
Doreen Green was born with a prehensile tail
that looks a whole lot like a squirrel's tail,

00:01:45.219 --> 00:01:49.850
and as she grew up, she discovered she had
various other rodent-like abilities, including

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:52.799
the power to understand and speak to squirrels
themselves.

00:01:52.799 --> 00:01:57.009
What really makes Squirrel Girl's origin particularly
interesting, though, is that Marvel has never

00:01:57.009 --> 00:01:59.700
fully pinned down exactly where her powers
came from.

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:03.720
Though her genetic makeup is altered from
that of a normal human, she isn't technically

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:06.300
a mutant in the same way that members of the
X-Men are.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:10.560
She's just ... different, and she's chosen
to use those differences for good.

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:15.110
Also, she managed to thoroughly defeat Doctor
Doom, one of the biggest bads of the entire

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:19.240
Marvel Universe, in her first appearance,
and she's pretty much been undefeated ever

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:19.780
since.

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:24.680
There's no way that a teenage girl with squirrel
powers taking down world-threatening supervillains

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:27.240
wouldn't make for a great on-screen origin
story.

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:31.620
Galactus, the nearly omnipotent "Devourer
of Worlds," has already appeared on the big

00:02:31.629 --> 00:02:36.489
screen once, but Fantastic Four: Rise of the
Silver Surfer used an incarnation that more

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:41.400
closely a massive cloud of energy rather than
the omnipotent humanoid that we've seen in

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:42.020
the comics.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:47.040
As the Fantastic Four prepare to enter the
MCU, it's time to give audiences the "real"

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:51.380
Galactus on the big screen, all while explaining
some of his epic cosmic background.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:55.780
Galactus was born Galan of Taa, an explorer
from an advanced planet that was one of the

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:59.600
last remaining civilizations in the universe
that existed before ours.

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:04.120
As his native universe imploded due to a kind
of crunching effect to prepare for another

00:03:04.129 --> 00:03:08.740
Big Bang, Galan decided to pilot a ship straight
into the heart of the "Cosmic Egg" that would

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:10.650
give birth to the next universe.

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:14.590
In short, he's the only survivor of the Big
Bang that created the Marvel universe as it

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:16.950
was first introduced in the 1960s.

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:21.159
Passing through that chaotic event led to
his rebirth as Galactus, a cosmic force of

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:25.820
nature scarier than Thanos who survived by
consuming the life force of entire worlds.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:30.020
We'd love to see a character that grand and
paradigm-shifting in live-action.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:35.280
The Hulk's hard-hitting gamma bombshell cousin
is about to get her own series on Disney+,

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:38.549
so there's a good chance we'll see some version
of She-Hulk's origin soon.

00:03:38.549 --> 00:03:42.439
That said, we still want to take a moment
to talk about why her superhero foundation

00:03:42.439 --> 00:03:46.360
is so great, and how it ties into the existing
MCU already.

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:50.629
Jennifer Walters was a meek but very intelligent
lawyer who just happened to be Bruce Banner's

00:03:50.629 --> 00:03:53.020
favorite cousin, thanks to their childhood
friendship.

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:57.111
When a crime boss' thugs tried to gun her
down while she was protecting a witness, Bruce

00:03:57.111 --> 00:04:01.329
struggled to save his cousin's life and realized
there was nothing he could do in the moment

00:04:01.329 --> 00:04:03.380
but give her a transfusion of his own blood.

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:07.940
Bruce's gamma-irradiated blood, coupled with
the emotional stress of the danger she was

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:09.960
in, transformed Jennifer into She-Hulk.

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:14.080
Over the next few decades, She-Hulk became
a standout character in her own right while

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:17.060
also remaining a key part of the overall Hulk
legacy.

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:20.720
Unlike Bruce, who, as you might've heard,
had some anger issues…

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:23.480
"I'm always angry."

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:27.680
...Jen has typically been fully in control
of herself as She-Hulk, and actually preferred

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:31.800
her glamorous green form, fighting crime and
practicing super-powered law.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:35.960
The balance of those two aspects of her character
has a lot of potential on the big and small

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:36.460
screens.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:40.860
If you're already familiar with the Marvel
Cinematic Universe and you hear the name "Captain

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:45.250
Britain," you might be expecting something
very similar to Captain America, like a World

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:50.050
War II hero specifically crafted to be a symbolic
champion for a country in crisis.

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:51.360
Well, you'd be wrong.

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:53.930
Captain Britain's story is actually a whole
lot weirder.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:58.240
Brian Braddock, was a grad student studying
physics who nearly died when the facility

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:00.810
he was working in was attacked by a supervillain.

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:06.050
As Brian bled to death, Merlin yes, that Merlin
approached him and asked him if he would become

00:05:06.050 --> 00:05:08.580
Britain's champion, which would save his life.

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:12.199
Braddock was given a choice between the Amulet
of Right and the Sword of Might, and he chose

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:13.200
the Amulet.

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:18.640
As a result, he was transformed into Captain
Britain, a superhero who guards his home nation

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:22.400
and, by extension, the world with his mystical
superhuman enhancements.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:26.150
The mystical nature of his origins, plus the
fact that there's actually a whole corps of

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:31.120
Captain Britain that protect the Marvel multiverse
from threats like the Fury, a super-terminator

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:35.380
that only exists to kill superheroes, would
make for a strange and wonderful journey in

00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:36.020
live-action.

00:05:36.740 --> 00:05:41.220
Ask any Thor fan which character they're still
most eager to see onscreen, and Beta Ray Bill

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:43.140
will almost always be at the top of the list.

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:48.780
Created by writer and artist Walt Simonson
in 1983, Bill first appeared as a new adversary

00:05:48.789 --> 00:05:53.020
for the god of thunder, but became something
much more than a simple enemy when he lifted

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:57.220
Thor's hammer, Mjolnir, and was found worthy
of the thunder god's power himself.

00:05:57.460 --> 00:06:00.640
As readers got to know him, Bill's tragic
story became clear.

00:06:00.820 --> 00:06:05.080
He was a member of an alien race whose home
was destroyed by the fire giant Surtur.

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:08.819
Bill was chosen as the great champion who
would lead his people to a new home, and he

00:06:08.819 --> 00:06:13.759
was given cybernetic enhancements in a painful
procedure that led to his ferocious appearance.

00:06:13.759 --> 00:06:17.970
Though Thor at first saw him as a threat,
Bill quickly proved himself to be an honorable,

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:21.509
well-intentioned warrior who was capable of
fighting as one of Thor's allies.

00:06:21.509 --> 00:06:26.140
He proved to be such a good guy, in fact,
that Odin even made him his own hammer, Stormbreaker.

00:06:26.140 --> 00:06:30.560
Bill's exploits made him a fan-favorite character,
and it's definitely time for him to make the

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:31.560
leap to live-action.

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:35.580
Part of Monica Rambeau's origin story has
already been told in the Marvel Cinematic

00:06:35.590 --> 00:06:39.550
Universe, because she appeared as a young
girl in 2019's Captain Marvel.

00:06:39.550 --> 00:06:44.509
Nicknamed "Lt. Trouble" by Carol Danvers,
Monica was the daughter of Carol's close friend,

00:06:44.509 --> 00:06:47.040
Maria, so she's a kind of niece to the superheroine.

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:48.040
"Auntie Carol?

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:49.560
Mom!

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:50.920
It’s Auntie Carol.

00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:52.940
I knew it.

00:06:52.940 --> 00:06:54.300
Everyone said you were dead.

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:55.960
But we knew they were lying."

00:06:56.780 --> 00:07:00.690
We know that Rambeau is showing up in the
Disney+ series WandaVision, but if she doesn't

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:05.389
get her superhero start there, then there's
always a possibility this child of the '90s

00:07:05.389 --> 00:07:07.680
could come into her own in a Captain Marvel
sequel.

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:10.120
Either way, her comic book origin is pretty
awesome.

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:14.759
In Marvel Comics, Monica Rambeau was bombarded
with extra dimensional energy from a weapon

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:16.210
created by a rogue scientist.

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:21.699
As a result, she's able to transform herself
into a being of pure energy across the electromagnetic

00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:22.200
spectrum.

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:26.940
This power has granted her a phenomenal level
of strength, even when compared to other superheroes,

00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:28.560
and she's wielded it well.

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:32.479
Monica has led the Avengers at certain points
in her comics career, and she's seen many

00:07:32.479 --> 00:07:37.210
different aliases, including her time as the
second Captain Marvel and her current codename,

00:07:37.210 --> 00:07:37.800
Spectrum.

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:41.140
Seeing her fight side-by-side with Carol would
be a wonderful development.

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:43.160
We just need the origin story.

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:47.380
Ms. Marvel is one of the most popular new
Marvel characters in the mainstream media

00:07:47.380 --> 00:07:48.200
of the past decade.

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:52.840
She's already appeared in video games, toy
lines, and animated shows, and is now set

00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:56.580
to find her way into live-action via a Disney+
series soon.

00:07:56.580 --> 00:08:00.200
It’s probably high time that her origin
story made it onto a screen someplace.

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:04.700
After all, we're living in a time when superhero
movies have sparked the most intense fandom

00:08:04.700 --> 00:08:09.440
in years, which makes Ms. Marvel herself one
of the easiest heroes for young fans to relate

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:09.940
to.

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:14.740
Kamala Khan is a Pakistani-American girl who
grew up in New Jersey and developed various

00:08:14.740 --> 00:08:19.610
nerdy interests, including a love of various
superheroes, particularly Carol Danvers, who

00:08:19.610 --> 00:08:21.700
in the comics was originally named Ms. Marvel.

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:26.479
One night, Kamala was exposed to the Terrigen
Mist that gives the Inhumans their powers,

00:08:26.479 --> 00:08:30.919
revealing the she herself had Inhuman blood
and was capable of gaining super powers herself

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:31.420
through "Terrigenesis."

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:35.440
When she emerged again, Kamala found that
she suddenly had the ability to morph her

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:39.849
body into any shape she could imagine, from
stretching out her limbs to "embiggened" size

00:08:39.849 --> 00:08:42.229
to enlarging to completely altering her appearance.

00:08:42.229 --> 00:08:46.570
With her newfound powers, she took up the
name of Ms. Marvel and began to fight crime.

00:08:46.570 --> 00:08:51.070
It's a great story, born out of superhero
fandom, and it'll be great to see some version

00:08:51.070 --> 00:08:53.260
of it arrive on the screen someday soon.

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:58.400
Amadeus Cho was created to infuse the Marvel
Universe with a new dose of youthful energy,

00:08:58.400 --> 00:08:59.340
in the vein of Spider-Man.

00:08:59.340 --> 00:09:04.040
Since his debut in 2004, he's gone on to become
one of the most consistently entertaining

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:08.230
young heroes on the roster, and one whose
story has a whole lot of twists and turns.

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:12.740
The son of Korean immigrants, Amadeus displayed
signs of a near-superhuman intellect from

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:13.779
a very early age.

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:18.560
When he was a teenager, he entered a quiz
contest for young geniuses and easily won.

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:23.220
Unfortunately, the contest was actually a
trap for an evil mastermind named Pythagoras

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:27.160
Dupree to uncover and then kill people who
might prove smarter than him.

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:31.180
Amadeus' family was killed in the resulting
attempt on his life, and he ended up on the

00:09:31.180 --> 00:09:31.680
run.

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:35.600
While trying to make his way in the world,
he made some pretty powerful friends, first

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:37.720
traveling with the Hulk, and then with Hercules.

00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:42.500
He's since become much, much more than simply
a super genius, including taking over for

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:46.320
both of those heroes as the Prince of Power
and the Totally Awesome Hulk.

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:50.240
The idea of a kid whose only crime is being
really, really smart getting swept up in a

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:54.100
world of superheroes and villains with such
sudden ferocity is compelling in the same

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:55.820
way that Spider-Man's story is.

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:59.790
It also gives Marvel Studios an opportunity
to give Bruce Banner a new person to play

00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:03.040
mentor to as the MCU continues to grow and
expand.

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:07.110
The comics have even figured out one of the
hardest parts, which is making super-intelligence

00:10:07.110 --> 00:10:08.910
a power that works visually.

00:10:08.910 --> 00:10:13.600
Plus, since his mom shows up in Age of Ultron,
we already know that he exists in the MCU.

00:10:13.820 --> 00:10:17.980
Hopefully, it's only a matter of time before
Amadeus himself makes an appearance on the

00:10:17.980 --> 00:10:18.480
screen.

